<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Senegal River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> River flows from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> highlands to the Atlantic, forming much of the border between modern Senegal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>. Its valley was an important agricultural and trading zone at the southern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> profiles refer to it in describing the movements and territories of these states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/senegal-river.jpg" alt="Senegal River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WILLAV-FR · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WL-S%C3%A9n%C3%A9gal-Rosso-Travers%C3%A9e_du_fleuve_S%C3%A9n%C3%A9gal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Within some seventy years they ruled a territory stretching roughly three thousand kilometres, from the <b>Senegal River</b> to the Ebro in northern Spain.</blockquote><a href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>France had held Saint-Louis and Gorée on the Senegalese coast since the seventeenth century, and from the 1850s Governor Louis Faidherbe expanded the colony of Senegal up the <b>Senegal River</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/french-west-africa">French West Africa · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After Sundiata's death around 1255, his successors, among them Mansa Uli, expanded the empire towards the <b>Senegal River</b> and opened ties with the wider Islamic world; Uli made the pilgrimage to Mecca.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Majorcan sailor Jaume Ferrer set out from Majorca to find the &quot;River of Gold&quot;, the <b>Senegal River</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-10">10 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Its territory lay around Aleg and along the right bank of the <b>Senegal River</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-brakna">Emirate of Brakna</a></li><li><blockquote>Gum arabic, sold to the French at <b>Senegal River</b> posts and to the Dutch and English at Portendick, was their main source of wealth.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-trarza">Emirate of Trarza</a></li></ul></section>
